# Notion credentials for local development.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or edit `.env`) and paste your token. `.env` is git-ignored; this example
# file is committed and must never hold a real token.
#
# Any of these forms works:
#
#   NOTION_TOKEN=ntn_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#   NOTION_TOKEN=secret_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx   # legacy token format
#
# A `.env` file that contains nothing but the token, with no `NOTION_TOKEN=` prefix at all, is also
# accepted, because that is what pasting a token into a file usually looks like:
#
#   ntn_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Optional. Without it the app reads the most recently edited page the integration can see.
# A page ID (dashed or not) or a full notion.so URL both work.
#
#   NOTION_PAGE_ID=1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d
#   NOTION_PAGE_ID=https://www.notion.so/Workspace/Architecture-1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d
#
# Remember to share the page with the integration in Notion, otherwise Notion answers 404.
